{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"prompt\": \"Use case: stylized-concept. Create a final Minecraft builder reference sheet refining the attached Sears Modern Homes concept (image-3 is the edit target; image-1 is the mood board). Landscape 3:2, plain warm light background, crisp vanilla Minecraft voxel blocks, skilled human builder quality, no characters or animals. TWO MAIN VIEWS SIDE BY SIDE: LEFT straight-on orthographic NORTH front elevation of the entire eight-house row; RIGHT NORTH-EAST three-quarter view of the SAME entire row at the SAME SCALE. Both views include all eight houses in identical order, no omissions. Use generous empty space below for enlarged construction details, keeping the two long rows readable. Small labels 0 Magnolia, 1 Alhambra, 2 Vallonia, 3 Puritan, 4 Cornell, 5 Stanford, 6 Winona, 7 Craftsman. Preserve the prior coordinated white, cream, sage, pale yellow, grey and brown colors, gardens, paired/triple framed double-hung windows, deep porches and house identities.\\n\\nExact grid: each row is 128 blocks along x, eight 16-wide plots; plot i x=16*i..16*i+15, z=5..24 (20 deep). Road z=0..2 gravel, sidewalk z=3..4 smooth_stone. Each house faces north, has a lawn to the sidewalk and centered front walk; all eaves, masonry and shrubs inside its plot. No front fence. Same low oak_leaves hedge on rear and sides. Modest gardens. Ground floor at most one block above lawn.\\n\\nCorrect the three principal shortcomings of the prior concept: (1) Puritan must have a strongly legible DUTCH GAMBREL, steep lower slopes and shallow upper slopes with visible angle breaks, long wide shed dormer; Cornell roof must remain LOW hipped with small hipped dormer. (2) Alhambra must have a CURVED SHAPED MISSION PARAPET approximated with stepped vanilla blocks, raised central curved silhouette with low shoulders, NOT a triangular stepped gable; deeply recessed THREE ROUND ARCH porch openings approximated with stairs/slabs, NOT a timber pergola. (3) All entrances must use half-step slab approaches, NOT stair stoops, and chimneys need open constant-width wall-integrated shafts rather than capped decorative stacks.\\n\\nHouse specifics: 0 Magnolia white Georgian Colonial Revival, grandest, two-and-half storeys, symmetrical FIVE bays, full-height white quartz_pillar portico columns, balcony over central door, side-gabled dark roof with three dormers. 1 Alhambra two-storey white_terracotta stucco, shaped Mission parapets and brick red tiled roof edges, triple arcaded porch. 2 Vallonia sage green_terracotta, one-and-half storeys, side-gabled roof sweeping over full-width porch, broad dormer, tapered posts on brick piers, spruce knee braces and exposed trapdoor rafter tails. 3 Puritan pale birch clapboard Dutch Colonial with true gambrel and long shed dormer, small columned pediment entry. 4 Cornell light_gray_terracotta two-storey cube, low hipped roof, hipped front dormer, full-width porch with square columns. 5 Stanford white Cape Cod, one-and-half storeys, steep side-gabled roof, TWO gabled dormers, central chimney, central door and dark shutters. 6 Winona cream smooth_sandstone, small ONE-storey front-gabled cottage with small porch under gable, visibly lowest and simplest. 7 Craftsman two-storey front-gabled, spruce shingle upper floor and sage lower clapboard, broad porch on stone piers, wide bracketed eaves.\\n\\nShow actual block-sized depth, proud trim, recessed openings, stairs/slab roof verges and eaves, ridge, fences, walls, trapdoors and lanterns. Only exact Minecraft 1.21.1 materials: birch_planks, white_terracotta, green_terracotta, light_gray_terracotta, smooth_sandstone, smooth_sandstone_stairs, smooth_sandstone_slab, quartz_pillar, quartz_stairs, quartz_slab, spruce_planks, spruce_stairs, spruce_slab, spruce_fence, spruce_trapdoor, spruce_door, deepslate_tiles, deepslate_tile_stairs, deepslate_tile_slab, bricks, brick_stairs, brick_slab, brick_wall, stone_bricks, s